+
+**Confirm / back differ from upstream in this port.** Upstream confirms on
+`I_RETURN` *and* `I_ACTION_M` and backs out only on Esc / `I_MENUS`, which on a
+gamepad means B and X both confirm, A does nothing, and only Start goes back.
+Here **`I_ACTION_M` / `I_ACTION_ALWAYS` (X / A) confirm** and **`I_RETURN` (B)
+backs out**, alongside Esc and Start — the console convention. Every caller
+already handles the `1000` sentinel as back/cancel, including the main menu,
+where it resumes the game rather than quitting. `ChoosePlayerName` runs its own
+loop and confirms on `I_FIRE`, so it is unaffected.
 
